---
layout: changelog
title: "Run functions on an interval"
date: 2026-10-09
description: "Functions can now run every N minutes on an interval, as an alternative to cron expressions. Appwrite picks when within each interval the function runs."
tags: functions, console, sdk
---

Functions can now run on an **interval** as well as a cron expression. Set an interval in minutes, and Appwrite runs your function once in each interval, at a fixed time it picks for that function. Functions with the same interval no longer all start at the same moment.

- **Interval**: every N minutes, for work that needs to run regularly but not at an exact time.
- **Cron**: exact times, for work tied to the clock, such as a report at 09:00 on Mondays.

Choose **Interval** in your function's **Settings** > **Schedule**, or pass `interval` to `functions.create` and `functions.update` in the latest Server SDKs. On Appwrite Cloud, intervals start at 1 minute on paid plans and 60 minutes on the Free and Education plans. Cron expressions are unchanged on every plan.

